# Build context for the client is Client/ (see docker-compose.yml / `docker
# build -f Client/Dockerfile Client`). Anything listed here never reaches the
# build context, which matters more than usual for this image specifically:
# node_modules here is whatever npm resolved on the HOST (Windows binaries for
# any native deps, arbitrary local state) - the `deps` stage in Dockerfile
# runs its own `npm ci` inside the Linux build container, so shipping the
# host's copy in would either be dead weight or, worse, a mismatched native
# binary silently shadowing the one npm ci would have installed.
node_modules/

# Next.js build output - regenerated by `npm run build` inside the image;
# shipping a stale host-built .next in would defeat the point of building it
# fresh (and standalone/ output layout can vary by Next.js version).
.next/
out/

# Env / secrets - NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are baked in at build time via
# docker-compose's build args instead, never by copying a real .env(.local)
# into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.local.example

# Version control / editor / OS cruft
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log

# Docker-related files themselves
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# Docs not needed in the image
*.md
